the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    Benutzungsberechtigung holds for *a case*.
    the answer to Benutzungsberechtigung for *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Benutzungsberechtigung would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r4_12_accept_own_text_without_uri includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/accept-own-text-without-uri.ruml".

the text of text 3f2c9a1e4b7d4e0f9a6c1b2d3e4f5a6b is at "sources/text_3f2c9a1e4b7d4e0f9a6c1b2d3e4f5a6b.txt".

rule node_1 with provenance text 3f2c9a1e4b7d4e0f9a6c1b2d3e4f5a6b:
Benutzungsberechtigung holds for a case if
    the answer to Benutzungsberechtigung for the case is true.

% Until a person answers, RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Benutzungsberechtigung holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the answer to Benutzungsberechtigung for the case is a truth value
    and Benutzungsberechtigung would hold for the case.

scenario generated_1 is, as stated in "accept-own-text-without-uri.ruml" at generated_1:
    % no data
    node_1 expects answers ["Benutzungsberechtigung holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Benutzungsberechtigung holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.

scenario generated_2 is, as stated in "accept-own-text-without-uri.ruml" at generated_2:
    % every leaf answered yes
    the answer to Benutzungsberechtigung for case 1 is true.
    node_1 expects answers ["Benutzungsberechtigung holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers [].

scenario generated_3 is, as stated in "accept-own-text-without-uri.ruml" at generated_3:
    % the leaf 1 answered no, the others yes
    the answer to Benutzungsberechtigung for case 1 is false.
